#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# ordered

#% text
# `ordered(xs)` gives `true` when the elements of `xs` are in the canonical order; `ordered(xs, by)` when `by(a, b)` holds for each pair of neighbours.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
ordered([1, 2, 2, 5])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
ordered([3, 1, 2])
#% output
#= false

#% cell
ordered([5, 3, 1], (a, b) => a > b)
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# After sorting, a list is ordered:

#% cell
ordered(sort([c, a, b]))
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sort`, `is_ordered`, `sort_by`
